 "description": "West sectors band-boxed (WW). Three waves of Lanzarote (GCRR) arrivals for TERTO - 4, then 5, then 6 aircraft - from KORNO via ABODA-IBALU-ERMED-TOVRA-VEDOD and from TAKAV direct VEDOD, merging at VEDOD; and three waves of Casablanca (GMMN) arrivals for MARJA (then LAKAM) - 2, then 3, then 4 - from AMSEL, KORNO and RUNAX via ABODA. Letters of agreement: cleared FL250 at TERTO / MARJA, 10 NM in trail. The arrivals ask for descent near VEDOD / ABODA, not always in the order of the sequence. Overflights for Gran Canaria and Fuerteventura on the same axes, and traffic crossing the ABODA-MARJA leg, stay at their levels in the way of the descents; GMMN departures climb against the arrivals.",
 "design_notes": "GCRR waves at VEDOD about 2100, 3200, 4300 s; GMMN waves at ABODA about 700, 1800, 2900 s. Same-level merges (loss if left alone): RYR72TK/TOM4HB at VEDOD FL370 40 s apart, VLG81KP/EZY88QP FL370 22 s, RYR33VN/EXS7NC FL370 25 s, RAM949/RAM1471 at ABODA FL370 25 s. Descent requests come between 30 s and 5 min before the merge point, sometimes the follower first. In the way: IBE3518/EZY91WP/EWG14T (KORNO-ABODA at FL310/330 just after each GMMN wave), BAW2581/NOZ418/SAS77K (RUNAX-IBALU crossing ABODA-MARJA at FL330/310), TOM67G/RYR8C/TOM2DM/TAP1129 (GCLP/GCFV on the TERTO axes), TAP1066 head-on on MARJA-ABODA at FL320, RAM1290 GMMN departure climbing to FL360 against GMMN wave 2, RAM2210 (SALCA-IBALU) climbing to FL350 into GCRR wave 3 at IBALU, BCS51 northbound asking FL400 as the TAKAV stream at FL390 crosses it.",
